---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBand from '../../components/layout/ContactBand.astro';
import ProjectMetadata from '../../components/project/ProjectMetadata.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';
import '../../styles/askwill.css';

const project = projects.find((item) => item.slug === 'askwill');
if (!project) throw new Error('AskWill project record is missing.');

const comparisons = [
  {
    id: 'services', title: 'Services', index: '01', width: 560, height: 680,
    summary: 'Service directory → symptom-led service guide.',
    why: 'The rebuilt Services page lets homeowners start with problems such as hard water, staining, odour, or low pressure, then points them toward the relevant service.',
    v1: '/assets/projects/askwill/services-v1-detail.webp',
    v2: '/assets/projects/askwill/services-v2-detail.webp',
    v1Alt: 'Recovered Wix Services page showing a catalogue of water-treatment and well services.',
    v2Alt: 'Final-stage rebuild preview of the Services page showing symptom-led service routing.',
  },
  {
    id: 'repair', title: 'Water Softener Repair', index: '02', width: 480, height: 320,
    summary: 'Service information → symptom-led repair and replacement guidance.',
    why: 'The rebuilt page starts with common symptoms and makes the repair-versus-replacement decision easier to follow.',
    v1: '/assets/projects/askwill/repair-v1-detail.webp',
    v2: '/assets/projects/askwill/repair-v2-detail.webp',
    v1Alt: 'Recovered Wix Water Softener Repair page with a sales-oriented service introduction.',
    v2Alt: 'Final-stage rebuild preview of Water Softener Repair with symptom-led repair-first guidance.',
  },
  {
    id: 'contact', title: 'Contact', index: '03', width: 560, height: 680,
    summary: 'Form-first contact page → direct call, email, and form options.',
    why: 'The rebuilt page keeps direct contact with Will visible and makes the form one option rather than the whole experience.',
    v1: '/assets/projects/askwill/contact-v1-detail.webp',
    v2: '/assets/projects/askwill/contact-v2-detail.webp',
    v1Alt: 'Recovered Wix Contact page centred on a conventional contact form.',
    v2Alt: 'Final-stage rebuild preview of Contact with direct-to-owner paths and a structured handoff.',
  },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rebuilding AskWill.ca"
  description="A full website rethink for a family-run water-service business, covering structure, content, SEO, privacy, and QA."
  canonicalPath={project.route}
>
  <article class="askwill-case">
    <header class="askwill-hero">
      <h1>Rebuilding AskWill.ca</h1>
      <p class="askwill-lede">I built the original AskWill site in Wix and maintained it for several years. It worked well, although visually it had a bit of an “amateur PowerPoint deck” vibe. Over that time, I conducted usability testing and monitored customer feedback and GA4 data to identify opportunities for improvement. By the time I rebuilt it, I had a pretty good idea of what I wanted to change.</p>
      <ProjectMetadata tags={project.tags} />
      <dl class="askwill-facts" aria-label="Project context">
        <div><dt>Business</dt><dd>Family-run water-treatment and well-services business</dd></div>
        <div><dt>My role</dt><dd>Designed and led the rebuild</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Result</dt><dd>19-page site now live at AskWill.ca</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <section class="askwill-section" aria-labelledby="clearest-change">
      <div class="askwill-intro">
        <div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Services</p><h2 id="clearest-change">Starting with the problem</h2></div>
        <p>Version 1 already had detailed service pages, but customers often knew the problem they were seeing before they knew which service or equipment they needed.</p>
      </div>
      {comparisons.slice(0, 1).map((comparison) => (
        <figure class="askwill-comparison" aria-labelledby={`${comparison.id}-comparison-title`}>
          <div class="askwill-comparison-copy"><div><p class="askwill-index">{comparison.index}</p><h3 id={`${comparison.id}-comparison-title`}>{comparison.title}</h3><p class="askwill-summary">{comparison.summary}</p></div><p>{comparison.why}</p></div>
          <div class="askwill-compare-grid">
            <div class="askwill-panel"><p class="askwill-panel-label">V1 · Wix</p><img src={comparison.v1} alt={comparison.v1Alt} width={comparison.width} height={comparison.height} loading="eager" decoding="async" /></div>
            <div class="askwill-panel"><p class="askwill-panel-label">V2 · Rebuild</p><img src={comparison.v2} alt={comparison.v2Alt} width={comparison.width} height={comparison.height} loading="eager" decoding="async" /></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Real screenshots from the original Wix site and the final-stage Version 2 preview.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="askwill-section" aria-labelledby="maintenance-title">
      <div class="askwill-intro"><div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Version 1</p><h2 id="maintenance-title">What maintaining the first site taught me</h2></div><p>Maintaining the first site gave me a clear list of requirements for the rebuild.</p></div>
      <div class="askwill-decisions" role="list">
        <div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Small layout changes could take too much work and affect nearby elements.</p><p><span>V2</span>Reusable components and explicit CSS rules.</p></div>
        <div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Desktop and mobile layouts could behave differently than expected.</p><p><span>V2</span>Defined responsive rules and repeatable viewport testing.</p></div>
        <div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Changes were difficult to review before publishing.</p><p><span>V2</span>Source control, tests, and branch-based review.</p></div>
        <div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Customers often described a problem before naming a service.</p><p><span>V2</span>Let visitors start with the problem they were seeing while keeping the full service list available.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="askwill-section" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
      <div class="askwill-intro askwill-intro--single"><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Customer journey</p><h2 id="journey-title">Making it easier to know where to start</h2></div>
      <ol class="askwill-journey">
        <li><span>01</span><strong>Notice a problem</strong><p>Start with what the homeowner can actually observe.</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><strong>Find the relevant service</strong><p>Use those symptoms to point toward the most relevant service.</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><strong>Understand the decision</strong><p>Explain choices such as repair versus replacement and treatment versus supply.</p></li>
        <li><span>04</span><strong>Talk directly with Will</strong><p>Give visitors a direct way to ask when the right next step is unclear.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="askwill-section" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
      <div class="askwill-intro askwill-intro--single"><h2 id="proof-title">Two more changes</h2></div>
      <div class="askwill-comparison-stack">
        {comparisons.slice(1).map((comparison) => (
          <figure class="askwill-comparison" aria-labelledby={`${comparison.id}-comparison-title`}>
            <div class="askwill-comparison-copy"><div><p class="askwill-index">{comparison.index}</p><h3 id={`${comparison.id}-comparison-title`}>{comparison.title}</h3><p class="askwill-summary">{comparison.summary}</p></div><p>{comparison.why}</p></div>
            <div class="askwill-compare-grid">
              <div class="askwill-panel"><p class="askwill-panel-label">V1 · Wix</p><img src={comparison.v1} alt={comparison.v1Alt} width={comparison.width} height={comparison.height} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
              <div class="askwill-panel"><p class="askwill-panel-label">V2 · Rebuild</p><img src={comparison.v2} alt={comparison.v2Alt} width={comparison.width} height={comparison.height} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
            </div>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="askwill-section" aria-labelledby="system-title">
      <div class="askwill-intro"><div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">The rebuild</p><h2 id="system-title">Structure, SEO, and QA</h2></div><p>I defined the site structure, content, SEO requirements, and QA criteria, then reviewed the implementation against those requirements.</p></div>
      <div class="askwill-three">
        <div><p class="askwill-mini">Site structure</p><ul><li>Problem-led service paths</li><li>Clearer distinctions between related services</li><li>Direct contact with Will</li></ul></div>
        <div><p class="askwill-mini">SEO migration</p><ul><li>Preserved established service URLs</li><li>Redirected legacy Wix routes</li><li>Kept organic and paid-search pages separate</li></ul></div>
        <div><p class="askwill-mini">QA</p><ul><li>Source-controlled review</li><li>Responsive viewport testing</li><li>Automated source and browser checks</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="askwill-section" aria-labelledby="validation-title">
      <div class="askwill-intro askwill-intro--single"><p class="askwill-eyebrow">QA</p><h2 id="validation-title">Testing the rebuild</h2></div>
      <div class="askwill-proof" aria-label="AskWill rebuild validation evidence">
        <div><strong>19</strong><span>pages in the build</span></div>
        <div><strong>199</strong><span>source tests</span></div>
        <div><strong>0</strong><span>automated failures</span></div>
        <div><strong>Firefox + WebKit</strong><span>browser checks</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="askwill-note">Some checks, including physical-device and assistive-technology review, still require manual testing.</p>
      <p class="askwill-live-result">The rebuilt site is now live at AskWill.ca.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <ContactBand />
</BaseLayout>
